---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Lock Change in Delaware | Lock Replacement Service | 1st Capital Locksmith"
  description="Professional lock change and lock replacement service throughout Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith replaces door locks for homes and businesses across Kent County — all lock types, on-site service, upfront pricing. Call (302) 735-0050."
>

  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="bg-white border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-3">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 flex-wrap">
        <li>
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Home</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <a href="/services/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Services</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <span class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold">Lock Change</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Schema: Breadcrumbs -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Lock Change", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/lock-change/" }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: Service -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Lock Change in Delaware",
    "description": "Professional lock change and lock replacement services for residential and commercial properties throughout Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith replaces door locks of all types on-site across Kent County — deadbolts, knob locks, lever handles, and more.",
    "provider": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "1st Capital Locksmith",
      "telephone": "+13027350050",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "addressLocality": "Dover",
        "addressRegion": "DE",
        "addressCountry": "US"
      }
    },
    "areaServed": {
      "@type": "State",
      "name": "Delaware"
    },
    "serviceType": "Lock Change"
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: FAQ -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does a lock change cost in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The cost of a lock change depends on the type of lock, the brand of replacement hardware, and the number of doors. We provide a clear upfront quote before any work begins. Call (302) 735-0050 for a fast estimate specific to your situation."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the difference between a lock change and rekeying?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Rekeying changes the internal pin configuration of your existing lock so old keys stop working — it's faster and less expensive, and the hardware stays in place. A lock change replaces the entire lock with new hardware. Lock change is the right choice when the existing lock is damaged, worn out, low quality, or when you want to upgrade to a different type or brand."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "When should I change my locks instead of rekeying them?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Change your locks when: the existing hardware is damaged or worn; you want to upgrade to a higher security grade; you want a different lock type (e.g., adding a deadbolt or switching to a keypad); after a break-in where the lock was compromised; or when the lock is simply too old and a rekey won't restore reliable performance."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can you change my locks the same day I call?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "In most cases, yes. Our mobile locksmiths carry common replacement hardware on their vehicles and can perform lock changes throughout Delaware often on the same day. Call (302) 735-0050 and we'll let you know our availability."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you change locks for rental properties and landlords in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. We regularly work with landlords and property managers throughout Delaware who need lock changes between tenants, after a lease dispute, or when a tenant fails to return keys. We can service multiple properties and offer efficient scheduling for portfolio landlords."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can you change the locks on my business in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Absolutely. We change commercial door locks for offices, retail spaces, warehouses, and other business properties throughout Delaware. We carry commercial-grade hardware and can schedule service around your business hours to minimize disruption."
        }
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative min-h-[340px] md:min-h-[550px] flex items-center text-white py-10 md:py-20"
    style="background-image: url('/images/lock-change-service.jpg'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/72"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-6 z-10">
      <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-xs md:text-sm mb-2 md:mb-4">Lock Change Services — Delaware</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-3 md:mb-6 max-w-3xl leading-tight">
        Professional Lock Change in Delaware — New Locks, Complete Peace of Mind
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm md:text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-5 md:mb-8">
        Moving into a new home? Upgrading old hardware? Dealing with a security concern? 1st Capital Locksmith provides fast, professional lock change service for homes and businesses throughout Delaware — all lock types, on-site replacement, and upfront pricing every time.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <a
          href="tel:3027350050"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-bold text-base md:text-lg hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
        >
          Call (302) 735-0050
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact/"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-white px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-semibold text-sm md:text-base hover:bg-white hover:text-[#1A1F22] transition"
        >
          Get a Free Quote
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Bar -->
  <section class="bg-[#0E1B2F] py-8">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">All Lock Types</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Deadbolts, Knobs, Levers & More</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Same-Day Service</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Hardware Stocked On Our Vehicles</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Mobile</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">We Come Directly to Your Property</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Upfront Pricing</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Clear Quote Before We Start</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Delaware's Lock Change Experts</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6 leading-snug">
            Lock Change & Lock Replacement Service Throughout Delaware
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sometimes rekeying isn't enough. When your locks are old, worn, damaged, or simply not up to the security standard your property deserves, changing them entirely is the right call. A fresh set of quality locks — properly selected and correctly installed — is one of the most reliable ways to take control of who has access to your home or business.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            1st Capital Locksmith provides professional lock change service for residential and commercial properties throughout Delaware. We carry a selection of quality replacement hardware and handle the full job on-site — removing old locks, fitting new hardware, testing operation, and leaving your property more secure than we found it. We also make sure the new lock fits your door correctly and that the strike plate is properly reinforced.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Whether you need one door lock changed or every exterior lock on your property replaced, we serve homeowners, renters, landlords, and business owners throughout Dover, Milford, Smyrna, Camden, Harrington, and all of Kent County, Delaware.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Photo Slot 1 -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-[#F8F8F5] aspect-[4/3] flex items-center justify-center">
            <img
              src="/images/lock-change-service.jpg"
              alt="Professional lock change service on a residential front door in Delaware"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
              width="600"
              height="450"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6">When You Need a Lock Change:</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {[
                "Moving Into a New Home or Apartment",
                "Lost or Stolen House Keys",
                "Tenant Moved Out — Lock Change Needed",
                "After a Break-In or Attempted Break-In",
                "Old, Worn, or Damaged Locks",
                "Upgrading to Higher Security Hardware",
                "Switching to a Keypad or Smart Lock",
                "Keys Given to Someone You No Longer Trust",
                "Post-Divorce or Roommate Change",
                "Commercial Tenant Turnover",
              ].map((item) => (
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-700">
                  <span class="w-6 h-6 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3">
                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  {item}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
              <a
                href="tel:3027350050"
                class="w-full inline-flex justify-center items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 text-white font-bold hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
              >
                Call (302) 735-0050 Now
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Lock Change Situations We Handle</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">
          Lock Change & Replacement Services in Delaware
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          There are many reasons to change your locks — and not all of them involve an emergency. Here's a detailed look at the most common lock change situations we handle for residents and businesses throughout Delaware.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8">

        <!-- Moving Into a New Home -->
        <div id="new-home" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 9.75L12 3l9 6.75V21a1 1 0 01-1 1H4a1 1 0 01-1-1V9.75z" />
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 22V12h6v10" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Lock Change When Moving Into a New Home in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Moving into a new home is one of the most common — and most important — reasons to change your locks. The previous owners, former tenants, real estate agents, contractors, cleaning crews, and anyone else who ever had a key to that property could still have a working copy. You have no way of knowing how many keys are out there, and the only way to truly take control of who can enter your home is to start fresh with new hardware.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith helps new homeowners and renters throughout Delaware get their new homes secured properly. In many cases, <a href="/services/lock-rekeying/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">rekeying the existing locks</a> is a fast and cost-effective solution if the hardware is in good condition. But if the locks are old, worn, low-quality builder-grade hardware, or if you simply want the peace of mind that comes with brand-new locks, we can replace every exterior lock on your home in a single visit.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We recommend scheduling your lock change the same day as your move-in, or even before you bring in your furniture and belongings. It's a small investment that pays for itself in the security and peace of mind it provides from your very first night in a new home.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Lost or Stolen Keys -->
        <div id="lost-keys" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 7a2 2 0 012 2m4 0a6 6 0 01-7.743 5.743L11 17H9v2H7v2H4a1 1 0 01-1-1v-2.586a1 1 0 01.293-.707l5.964-5.964A6 6 0 1121 9z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Lock Change After Lost or Stolen Keys in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Losing your keys — or having them stolen — creates an immediate security concern. If your keys had any kind of identifying information attached to them (a tag with your address, a keychain from a local business, or anything that could connect the key to your home), you should act quickly. Even if there's no obvious identification, the possibility that someone has both a key and the motivation to use it is a real risk that isn't worth leaving unaddressed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Rekeying is often the fastest and most affordable option in a lost key situation — it prevents the lost key from working without replacing the entire lock hardware. However, if your current locks are already past their prime, this is a good opportunity to upgrade to better hardware at the same time. 1st Capital Locksmith carries replacement hardware and can do either on the same visit.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Don't let a lost key sit as an open security question. Call us and we'll get your home re-secured quickly throughout Delaware, with upfront pricing before we start.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tenant Turnover / Rental Properties -->
        <div id="rental" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17 20h5v-2a4 4 0 00-4-4H4a4 4 0 00-4 4v2h5m6 0v-4m0 0a4 4 0 10-8 0m8 0a4 4 0 108 0" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Lock Change for Rental Properties & Tenant Turnover in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Every responsible landlord changes or rekeys the locks between tenants — full stop. No matter how well a tenancy went, the outgoing tenant may have made copies of the keys that were never returned, and those copies are now in the hands of people you don't know. Protecting your next tenant — and your property — means ensuring no previous key will work when a new tenant moves in.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith works with landlords and property managers throughout Delaware to handle lock changes at tenant turnover, after lease disputes, and in situations where a tenant failed to return all keys at move-out. We're efficient, reliable, and understand the time pressure that comes with tenant turnovers — we work around your scheduling to get the property re-secured between occupancies.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              If you manage multiple rental properties in Kent County, give us a call. We offer consistent, reliable service across your portfolio and can build a working relationship that makes lock changes a seamless part of your turnover process.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- After Break-In -->
        <div id="after-break-in" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Lock Change After a Break-In in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              After a break-in, getting your property re-secured is the immediate priority. Any lock that was attacked — whether by kicking, picking, drilling, or prying — needs to be assessed and in most cases replaced. A lock that has been forcibly compromised may appear to function normally while having significantly reduced structural integrity and security capability. You can't rely on it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Beyond just replacing the damaged hardware, a break-in is also a clear signal to review the overall quality of every lock on your property. Burglars typically target the easiest entry point — but they'll move to the next easiest if the first fails. Upgrading from builder-grade hardware to quality Grade 1 deadbolts across all entry points is a smart response to a break-in.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              1st Capital Locksmith responds to post-break-in lock change calls throughout Delaware. We also assess and reinforce door frames and strike plates that may have been weakened during the forced entry — because a strong lock on a weakened frame is only as good as the frame. Call (302) 735-0050 and we'll get there as quickly as possible.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Security Upgrade -->
        <div id="upgrade" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Security Upgrade Lock Change in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Many homes in Delaware — particularly those built in the last decade or two — came with builder-grade locks as standard. These are typically ANSI Grade 3 hardware: the lowest security classification, designed to meet a minimum cost target rather than a maximum security standard. They're often straightforward to defeat, and they wear out faster than quality hardware.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Upgrading to ANSI Grade 1 <a href="/services/deadbolt-installation/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">deadbolts</a> and quality entry hardware is one of the highest-return security investments you can make in your home. The price difference between builder-grade and Grade 1 hardware is modest, but the difference in forced-entry resistance, pick resistance, and overall durability is significant. Many homeowners who have upgraded describe the change as noticeable — the hardware simply feels and operates like a different category of product.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              1st Capital Locksmith advises on and installs security upgrade lock replacements for homes and businesses throughout Delaware. Whether you want to upgrade one door or every lock on the property, we'll help you choose the right hardware for your security goals and budget.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Commercial Lock Change -->
        <div id="commercial" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 21V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v14M3 21h18M9 21v-4a1 1 0 011-1h4a1 1 0 011 1v4" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Commercial Lock Change in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Commercial properties have their own distinct lock change needs — employee turnover, management changes, security audits, lease transitions, and hardware that's reached the end of its service life are all common triggers. Keeping control of who has access to your business is an ongoing responsibility, and lock changes are a key part of that.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith changes commercial door locks for offices, retail stores, restaurants, warehouses, medical practices, and other business properties throughout Delaware. We carry commercial-grade hardware and can advise on the best options for your specific access control needs — from standard keyed deadbolts to keypad entry systems to locks that integrate with <a href="/services/master-key-systems/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key systems</a>.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We understand that commercial lock work needs to happen on your schedule. We'll work around your business hours, coordinate with your facilities team, and complete the work with minimal disruption to your operations. Call us at (302) 735-0050 to discuss your commercial lock change needs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Lock Change vs Rekey -->
        <div id="change-vs-rekey" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
